## 5 Battle-Tested BFCM Video Hook Formulas

### 1. The "Secret Insider Code" Hook
- **Visual**: Creator looking conspiratorially at their phone screen in low ambient lighting.
- **Script**: *"If you're planning on shopping the Black Friday sale on Friday... don't. Use the secret early access code **VIP30** right now before everything sells out."*
- **Why It Converts**: Exploits consumer FOMO and the desire for exclusivity.

### 2. The "Worst Gifts to Avoid" Hook
- **Visual**: Creator shaking their head and tossing generic gift items (socks, mugs) off-camera.
- **Script**: *"Stop buying people cheap novelty junk they will throw in the trash. Here are 3 gifts under $50 that my friends actually screamed when they opened."*
- **Why It Converts**: Positions your product as a thoughtful, high-value solution to a universal holiday dilemma.

### 3. The "Math Breakdown / Bundle Savings" Hook
- **Visual**: Split screen with physical product bundle on left and digital receipt / calculator on right.
- **Script**: *"Okay, math time. Individually, this kit costs $180. But right now for Cyber Week, they bundled all three with a travel case for $69. That is literally $1.15 a day."*
- **Why It Converts**: Rationalizes emotional purchases with objective cost justification.

### 4. The "Unboxing My Holiday Haul" ASMR Hook
- **Visual**: Crisp macro close-up of cutting open shipping tape, pulling out textured packaging, and hands-on tactile product display.
- **Script (or Subtitles only)**: *"The packaging alone is unreal. Look at this finish..."* (Heavy focus on crisp sound design and tactile satisfaction).
- **Why It Converts**: Delivers sensory satisfaction that mimics an in-person retail experience.

### 5. The "Inventory Warning" Scarcity Hook
- **Visual**: Fast-paced montage of warehouse packing or inventory alerts flashing red on screen.
- **Script**: *"If this shade is still in stock when you see this video, order it immediately. It sold out three times last November and shipping cutoffs are in 48 hours."*
- **Why It Converts**: Real scarcity prompts immediate checkout without price hesitation.

